WHOA. No wish for the Orb of Detection or a cloak of magic resistance?
You ascended without magic resistance? On your *first ascension*? Wow,
that's pretty amazing.

But seriously, if you *did* ascend without it, or don't know what it
is, listen up. Magic resistance is the hardest resistance in the game
to acquire, and it's worth spending your first wish to get it if you
don't have it, since it protects from most wizard-school spells
(including touch of death), polymorph traps, and death rays. See, the
only sources are the cloak of magic resistance, gray dragon scale
mail, Magicbane, or some of the lawful or neutral quest artifact.

Losing a character to Rodney's touch of death is beyond painful. If
you're a monk, that means either get one of the appropriate artifacts,
or wish for the cloak.
If you try one of the other classes, consider wishing for blessed
fixed greased +3 gray dragon scale mail next time you find a magic
lamp at Izchak's.




